.TH DANBY-GOLFDRIVE 1
.SH NAME
danby-golfdrive \- aerodynamic trajectory of a driven golf ball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/golfdrive
.SH MODEL
The drive includes gravity, quadratic drag, and backspin-induced Magnus lift.
Unlike a vacuum parabola, increasing lift can increase hang time while drag
reduces horizontal speed.  Integration ends at an interpolated ground impact.
.SH DISPLAY
The large plot shows height against carry distance and the smaller plot shows
speed against time.  Tracks alter ball speed, launch angle, drag, lift,
backspin, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/golfdrive.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
